                       "LPL", List Player Levels Utility
                                 for use with

                             The Immortal Struggle
        Created, programmed and copyright (C)1994 by Chris W. Rea [UL]
     A multiplayer online game for BBX, DLG-Pro, FalconCBCS, and Xenolink
                            Release Date: 09-Apr-94


                                How To Use LPL
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
     LPL  (which  stands  for List Player Levels) is a small utility for use in
conjunction  with  The  Immortal Struggle online game.  LPL will search through
the  "TIS_Players.dat" file in the current directory and then output a list, in
ascending order by Entity Level, all active entities found in the file.

     Why  is  this useful you ask?  If you would like to have a contest game of
T.I.S.  to last a definite period of time, such a utility helps in locating the
Entity  with  the  highest  Level  of  understanding in the game so they may be
designated the "winner".

     I  realize  that due to the nature of the game itself, a complete game may
last  for  a few weeks or a few months, or even longer, depending on the amount
of  competition  generated.   Using LPL you can tell after a definite period of
time  who  has  "won",  instead  of waiting for somebody to reach the apex of a
mountain and obliterate the continuum, which may take a long time.

     The  LPL command takes no arguments.  You must execute it in the directory
where the "TIS_Players.dat" file is located.  If it does not locate the file in
the  current directory it will tell you so.  Otherwise, it will read all active
(ie:   non-deleted/suicided)  entities  into memory, quicksort them using their
Level of understanding as primary sort key, and then output them.

     Have fun!

